  correlationId: req.correlationId,
});
```

## Security Guidelines

- Always hash passwords using bcrypt before storing
- Use JWT tokens with appropriate expiration times
- Implement refresh token mechanism for long-lived sessions
- Validate all user inputs to prevent SQL injection and XSS attacks
- Use parameterized queries (Prisma handles this automatically)
- Implement rate limiting to prevent abuse
- Use HTTPS in production
- Store sensitive configuration in environment variables
- Never commit secrets to version control
- Implement CORS with appropriate origin restrictions
- Sanitize file uploads and validate file types
- Implement proper authentication and authorization for all protected routes

## Performance Guidelines

- Use database indexes for frequently queried fields
- Implement pagination for list endpoints
- Use Prisma connection pooling
- Cache frequently accessed data (Redis recommended)
- Optimize database queries with proper includes and selects
- Use batch operations where possible
- Implement lazy loading for large datasets
- Monitor query performance and optimize slow queries
- Use CDN for static assets
- Compress responses with gzip

